	)
	(text_box "The LMV321 is a single channel op-amp. The current consumption should be around 130uA at\nmost for it and shouldn't be an issue for most designs.\n\nFor usage you'll want to set the Feedback and input resistors using the standard\nop-amp formula.\n\nOn the processing end of things the signal should be pretty close to rail-to-rail\nso assume:\n8 bit: 0-255, 10 bit: 0-1024, 12bit: 0-4096"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 114.3 129.54 0)
		(size 101.6 30.48)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1fd58b47-e84c-4988-8e98-6153a560bcae")
	)
	(text_box "Av(gain): -Rf/Rin\nVout: Av * Vin"
